  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum error in the measurement of resistance, current and time for which current flows in an electrical circuit are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>%</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math> respectively. The maximum percentage error in the detection of the dissipated heat will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Heat generated through resistance is given by,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></math></p><p>Therefore, the percentage error in the calculation can be found by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>%</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#916;</mi><mi>H</mi></mrow><mi>H</mi></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
